    "narrative": "LawDog enters today\u2019s slate with **Bryce Harper** (76.31) and **Lawrence Butler** (72.75) anchoring the offense as our clear top-tier options. **Bryce Harper** faces a favorable matchup against Eric Lauer, benefiting from a high xwOBA projection and an elite SP skill boost (+19%). Meanwhile, **Lawrence Butler** remains a priority start despite an assumed 8-hole assignment; he grades out exceptionally well due to the high-upside matchup against Merrill Kelly and a strong dynamic platoon advantage (+13%). **Luis Arraez** also provides a high-floor, high-efficiency play (69.53) against Seth Lugo, leveraging his batting order position and platoon edge to sustain our AVG category.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today involved **Drew Gilbert**, who sits on the bench with a respectable 52.34 score. While **Drew Gilbert** offers speed potential, he was squeezed out of the final lineup due to a suboptimal 8-hole projection and the optimizer\u2019s preference for the situational advantages offered by our starters. We are keeping a close watch on **Gavin Sheets**, who carries a 50.35 score but is being benched not just for efficiency reasons, but due to a 35% rain risk in his matchup against Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez. Every position player, including **Cal Raleigh**, **Yainer Diaz**, **Jonathan Aranda**, **Gleyber Torres**, **Geraldo Perdomo**, **Jeremiah Jackson**, **Taylor Ward**, **Dylan Beavers**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Daulton Varsho**, remains in \"Lineup Pending\" status; owners should monitor official confirmation, as any shift from our assumed batting orders could trigger a re-evaluation of the 40\u201359 point marginal starts.",
